[results]
The supplied section headings report qualitative outcomes rather than numeric values: NgTET modulated the abundance of T4 DNA modifications; this modulation altered bacterial cell lysis; temporal removal of DNA modifications enhanced CRISPR-Cas12 targeting of phage DNA; continuous removal prevented bacterial lysis; removal was reversible; NgTET-treated T4 DNA allowed efficient Cas-mediated phage DNA targeting in vivo; temporary removal enabled efficient phage T4 genome editing; and epigenetic cytosine modifications were common in phage genomes. No fold changes, LC-MS peak areas, survival percentages, p-values, or statistical significance values are provided in the supplied text.
[context]
