ent model, or statistical significance [(Catania et al., 2017-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/8a2d762c80b1ffec121b73ab3b97935eebd7523d), so it supports mass-spectrometric 5mC measurement but does not establish that the proposed combined restriction-digest/mass-spectrometry workflow is reproducible or transferable to E. coli C2523.",
  "suggested_action": "Most important, decouple the two measurements and state them separately: use LC-MS/MS nucleoside quantification to measure total 5mC, and optionally 5hmC and 5fC, in E. coli DNA after pBAD induction, with isotope-labeled internal standards, MRM transitions, linearity, recovery, limit of detection, biological and technical replicates, and statistical comparison among empty vector, M.SssI, M.MpeI, arabinose dose, and time points. Use methylation-sensitive restriction digestion, for example HpaII/MspI at CCGG or other CG-sensitive enzymes, only as a site-specific confirmation of DNMT activity, not as the primary genome-wide 5mC quantification. Second, add an orthogonal genome-wide mapping assay, such as Nanopore direct 5mC calling or whole-genome bisulfite sequencing, to map where M.SssI and M.MpeI methylate the E. coli genome, specifying platform, read depth, basecaller, methylation-calling tool, coverage, conversion efficiency, and multiple independent clones. Third, integrate the methylation measurements with the survival and mechanistic assays by measuring 5mC, 5hmC, 5fC, and ROS at the same arabinose induction times used for MMS, H2O2, cisplatin, alkB mutant, and TET co-expression experiments, align these time points with RNA-seq oxyR analysis, and use two-way or three-way ANOVA with effect sizes, confidence intervals, and false-discovery-rate correction to test DNMT, inducer, time, and repair-mutant interactions. Fourth, improve reproducibility by reporting all implementation details missing from the related work: DNA extraction and depurination/hydrolysis protocol, LC-MS instrument and parameters, restriction enzyme digest conditions, qPCR or fragment analysis for digested products, primer or probe design if PCR is used, and controls for arabinose toxicity, pBAD leakiness, DNMT protein expression, and McrABC-independent DNA degradation in C2523. Finally, if the hypothesis about 3mC off-target damage is central, add 3mC quantification by MS or targeted sequencing, but this is secondary to validating the 5mC quantification workflow.",
  "soundness_score": 5
